 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-- **Approximation Error:** As the number of quantiles $q$ approaches infinity, the PDF converges to a closed-form continuous distribution. Finite $q$ is an approximation [S1].
-- **KDE Fluctuations:** If the number of noise samples used to estimate the initial PDFs is small, the resulting KDE may be poor. This leads to significant fluctuations in the interpolated PDF results, especially for a high number of quantiles [S1].
